## Core Product Modules

### Dashboard
Hero: import operations. Primary CTAs: **Get Freight Quote** / **Start Import**.  
Primary metrics: Active Imports, In Transit, In Customs, Action Required, In Delivery, Freight Pending.  
**No** Active Trades / In Production / RFQ actions in primary Turkey experience.

### Priority Actions / Attention Required
Each attention item must carry: WHAT, WHY, OWNER, ACTION, STATUS, RESOLUTION.  
Ownership shown must match ownership data the system actually tracks. No fake automation.

### Start Import — Minimum entry models
- **A** — Existing Purchase Order
- **B** — Direct Import (no sourcing required)
- **C** — Freight-first

Turkey Importer users must NOT be required to go through RFQ or CommodityBid to start an import.

### My Imports
Each import card shows: import ID, supplier, origin/destination, shipment, current stage, ETA, freight/customs/delivery status, exception state, landed cost state, next action.  
One click into import workspace.

### Freight
State progression visible to user: Quote Requested → Offer Available → Selected → Booking Pending → Booking Confirmed → Shipment Created.

### Shipment Workspace
Single context view: shipment summary, container info, origin/destination, carrier/vessel, booking, tracking, ETA, timeline, documents, customs, inland delivery, POD, landed cost, exceptions.  
User must not search for the same shipment across multiple modules.

### Tracking Architecture
Provider must be behind an adapter abstraction — no hard-coded single provider.  
Tracking data becomes operational context (feeds Timeline, Exception, Control Tower).  
Graceful degradation when provider unavailable.

### Timeline
Cross-domain milestone view: Booking Confirmed → Container Gate In → Vessel Departed → ETA Updated → Vessel Arrived → Discharged → Customs Started → Customs Cleared → Ready for Pickup → Inland Delivery → Delivered → POD Confirmed.

### Exceptions
Severity: Info / Low / Medium / High / Critical.  
Lifecycle: OPEN → IN PROGRESS → RESOLVED.

Examples: ETA change, delay, stale tracking, missing document, customs readiness issue, customs action, inland delivery issue, POD missing, operational deadline.

### Control Tower
Answers: "Which imports need attention today?"  
Minimum: Active Imports, Need Attention, Customs Actions, Document Issues, Delivery Actions.  
Shares the same operational reality as the Exception system — no separate demo data.

### Documents
Operational component, not a file depot. Linked to import / PO / shipment / customs case / delivery.  
Document readiness calculable (e.g. B/L: MISSING → Customs: NOT READY).

### Customs
Buyer sees: customs case status, document readiness, broker status, customs milestones, clearance result.  
CTA: "Request DeMaxtore Customs" on eligible shipment. If case exists: "Open Customs".

**Shipment-level Turkey eligibility** (Turkey destination) is separate from **organisation-level operating model**.

### Broker Workspace
Broker has own execution surface: assigned customs cases, documents, readiness, requested information, customs progression, clearance status.  
Buyer must not see broker's internal margin / commercially sensitive data.

### Inland Delivery
CUSTOMS CLEARED → READY FOR PICKUP → TRUCKER ASSIGNED → INLAND DELIVERY → DELIVERED → POD.  
Visible on the same Import Journey.

### Trucker Workspace
Trucker: assigned deliveries, pickup, delivery status, delivery completion, POD.  
Buyer must not see internal carrier cost.

### POD
Linked to delivery / shipment / import / documents / timeline.  
DELIVERED → POD UPLOADED → POD CONFIRMED.

### Landed Cost
Components: product cost, freight, surcharges, insurance, customs-related costs, duties, taxes, broker costs, port/local charges, inland delivery, other eligible costs.  
Estimated vs. actual must be distinguished. No invented values.

