## Roles
- **Buyer** — importer customer
- **DeMaxtore Ops** — coordinates operation
- **Broker** — customs execution
- **Trucker** — inland delivery execution
- **Supplier** — source/document/order collaboration where needed

---

## UI/UX Principles

**No dead ends** — every customer-facing CTA must have a working flow behind it.

**Truthful UI** — system must not claim capabilities that are not implemented (e.g. live AIS tracking when only manual data exists). Simulated/manual data must be clearly distinguished.

**Customer language** — My Imports, Freight, Shipments, Customs, Deliveries, Documents, Landed Cost, Control Tower, Exceptions. Internal domain terminology must not leak to customer UI.

---

## E2E Golden Paths (Required)

**Import Golden Path:** PO → Start Import → Freight Quote → Offer → Booking → Shipment → Tracking/Timeline → Documents → Customs → Customs Cleared → Inland Delivery → Delivered → POD → Landed Cost

**Exception Golden Path:** ETA change → tracking event → timeline update → exception created → Control Tower Need Attention → owner/action context → resolved → audit trail

**Document → Customs:** Missing doc → customs NOT READY → doc provided → readiness updated → customs proceeds

**Customs → Delivery:** Customs Cleared → Ready for Pickup → Trucker → Pickup → Delivery → POD

**Landed Cost:** freight + customs-eligible costs + inland → landed cost calculation; no internal margin leak

**International Non-Regression:** International login → Dashboard → RFQ → CommodityBid → sourcing nav → PO → Inspection → Documents → Timeline → Shipment Tracking → Exceptions — all working, no Turkey copy/navigation leakage

